MenuBarTemplates is a lightweight, local macOS menu bar app for reusable email
templates. It stores templates on disk (no cloud, accounts, or sync), supports
placeholder resolution, and writes rich HTML plus a plain-text fallback to the
clipboard for pasting into Gmail, GoHighLevel, and similar tools.

How to use: build with `./scripts/build-app.sh` and run `open
dist/MenuBarTemplates.app`; run resolver checks with `swift run ResolverTests`.
Template data lives at
`~/Library/Application Support/MenuBarTemplates/templates.json`. Updates for
this project live in `updates/` per its CLAUDE.md conventions.

Status: adopted into AI Control on 2026-09-28. Existing, working Swift Package
(SwiftUI/AppKit/WebKit) with core template model, resolver, clipboard writer,
and menu bar UI.

In flight (paused 2026-09-28, both implemented + pushed, awaiting a human
visual check before closing):
- DOCK VISIBILITY — app shows a Dock icon only while its window is open
  (activation-policy toggle). See updates/2026-09-28 DOCK VISIBILITY - OPEN.
- APP ICON — white tile + copy/paste glyph for the Dock/Finder. See
  updates/2026-09-28 APP ICON - OPEN.

Known limitation: pasted inline/blob-backed images may not carry into every
receiving app (see README). See issues.txt for the running TODO list and the
INIT update for adoption details.
